r  sister isabella which seems to heal the  family's problems mirabelle finds a  vision perplexing though since she and  isabella don't get along  while mirabelle isn't thrilled with the  idea she's willing to do what it takes  to help her family so she seeks out  isabella with the intention of hugging  her as bruno's vision dictates  earlier mirabelle ruined a dinner at  which local hunk mariano was supposed to  propose to isabella so when mirabelle  tries to get that hug isabella responds  by yelling at mirabelle for destroying  her moment  but then isabella concedes she was only  willing to marry mariano because abuela  alma approved of the match she admits  she spent her whole life being as  perfect as possible for the good of the  family suppressing whole parts of  herself in the process  as isabella yells she sprouts flowers  until her anger reaches its apex and she  creates a cactus  she's delighted by her prickly and  imperfect creation and it makes her  wonder what else she can do with her  powers if she doesn't have to be perfect  she and mirabella sing what else can i  do as isabella further celebrates the  joys of embracing her true self  as isabella's song ends and she and  mirabelle arrive in the courtyard of the  modrical's house abuela alma is there to  greet them  isabella has spent the entirety of her  song exploring the limits of her powers  which means she created plants that  aren't beautiful but are a fuller  expression of who she really is  this has caused her to make a mess of  her dress and hair turning them from put  together perfection to a colorful  hodgepodge and abuela is furious to see  it  yet mirabelle ends up bearing the brunt  of abuela's ire when she once again  tries to express her concerns about the  magic in the house flickering out the  madrigal's gifts and their magical  houses powered by a candle that abuela  prayed to during her flight from her  original home 50 years ago in the time  since the candle has never gone out and  the magical miracle has become the  source of the madrigal's identity in the  community  so instead of taking her concerns  seriously abuela is angered by  mirabelle's repeated suggestions that  the candle could go out and the magic  could die abuela and mirabelle argue  fiercely and as they do  more cracks start to appear in the  foundation of the house to the  astonishment and horror of everyone in  the family  as a crack splits the ground between  granddaughter and grandmother mirabelle  springs into action the house starts to  crumble as mirabelle climbs to the open  window where the madrigal family's  magical candle sits the rest of the  family saves one another from falling  debris and runs from the house just as  mirabelle reaches the candle  only to find that for the first time it  has melted to a tiny husk  when the dust clears and the house is  nothing more than a pile of rubble  mirabelle is nowhere to be found  the family especially mirabelle's mother  and father don't know where she went and  spread out into the nearby mountains and  forest in the hopes of finding her  ultimately it's abuela alma who  discovers mirabelle sitting by the side  of a river that she hasn't gone near  since she arrived in their current home  half a century ago  now that the worst has come to pass  abuela's anger has dissipated but  mirabella is still hurt and defeated  abuela reveals that the river mirabella  sitting beside is where mirabelle's  grandfather abuela's husband pedro died  while trying to defend her and their  children from the people that forced  them to leave their original home  after the collapse of their house abuela  has come to realize she's been holding  on too tight to the family's miracle she  was so traumatized by the loss of her  husband that the idea of anything else  bad happening especially the loss of  another family member has caused her to  see the family's gifts as a lifeline  it's why she hasn't been able to  appreciate everything mirabelle 